# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the coconut test suite.
#
# The notify tests call libnotify's notify_notification_show(), which spawns a
# persistent GDBus worker thread. GLib's allocator is thread-safe, but TSan
# cannot see GLib's internal synchronization, so it reports data races on
# g_malloc/g_free between the main thread and the 'gdbus' thread. These are
# false positives — the same pattern is suppressed in GLib's own test suite.
#
# Suppress by GLib module name (frames are unsymbolized in CI, so the module
# name is what TSan matches) and by the notify test file (which appears in the
# previous-memory-access stack of every report).
race:libglib-2.0.so.0
race:tests/unit/notify_test.cpp
